able bound","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_141_q5_m1":["cnm_141","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_141","cnm_174","cnm_191","cnm_132","cnm_054"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7574fb983d56754f1627cf41"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D (14)","reason":"Reflect B across AC to B' and C across AB to C'. Then BE+DE+CD=B'E+ED+DC'≥B'C'. The angle B'AC' is 120°, so B'C'=sqrt(10²+6²-2·10·6 cos120°)=14. The segment B'C' crosses AC and AB, in that order, within the given sides, so equality is attainable.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_141"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2014_AMC_12A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_058","cnm_112","cnm_115"],"id":"double-reflection-elementary","label":"Straighten the path by reflection","methodDirectNodeIds":{"double-reflection-elementary":["cnm_141","cnm_132","cnm_054","cnm_137","cnm_140","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_141","cnm_132","cnm_054","cnm_137","cnm_140","cnm_174","cnm_058","cnm_112","cnm_115"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7574fb983d56754f1627cf41"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: R, P, S, Q","reason":"R uses chords in place of P's end arcs, so R<P. If the rink width is w and the straight-side height is h, the straight portions of P and S have lengths 2h and 2√(h²+w²). Unfolding Q's zigzags gives a straight-portion lower bound of 2√(h²+4w²). Their end arcs are identical, so P<S<Q. Hence R<P<S<Q.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_141"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2024_AMC_8_Q06","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_132","cnm_075"],"id":"common-arcs-and-unfolded-zigzags","label":"Compare common arcs and unfold the zigzags","methodDirectNodeIds":{"common-arcs-and-unfolded-zigzags":["cnm_054","cnm_141","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_054","cnm_141","cnm_174","cnm_0